# What language each published artifact is actually written in.
#
# Why this file exists: llms.txt is an English index, and it used to imply the
# work behind it was English too. It was not. Two of the three theory notes -- the
# payload inlined into /llms-full.txt -- were written in Chinese, as are four of
# the research pages. An agent told "the canonical index is English", handed the
# self-contained bundle, and given no inLanguage anywhere, got two thirds Chinese
# prose and no warning. That is the gap this closes.
#
# Both of those theory notes now have an English canonical edition, translated
# from the Chinese original, which is kept alongside it at the same base name
# with a `.zh.` infix. The bundle inlines BOTH editions of each -- a note is not
# translated to match the index it happens to be linked from, so the language of
# each inlined body is stated in its Source marker and is load-bearing. The four
# Chinese research pages are still Chinese-only, and are still marked `· 中文` in
# both indexes; do not let that marker rot into a decoration.
#
# Rules, in precedence order:
#
#   1. A `.zh.` infix in a filename means zh-Hans. It is the ONLY locale marker a
#      filename carries, and it always sits immediately before the final suffix:
#      `research/wave-backprop-en.zh.html`. The canonical sibling of any `.zh.`
#      file is its path with `.zh.` removed -- that one-line rule is what lets CI
#      check the two language editions of the index for set equality.
#
#      Note the awkward case, and do not "fix" it: `-en` in `wave-backprop-en` is
#      NOT a locale marker. It is a legacy part of that artifact's base name, and
#      it stays, because llms.txt promises in prose that the retracted claim is
#      kept "at its original URL". Renaming it to satisfy a naming scheme would
#      make the index lie about the one thing the tombstone exists to guarantee.
#      Hence its Chinese alternate is `wave-backprop-en.zh.html`.
#
#   2. An .html file already declares its language in <html lang>. That attribute
#      is authoritative. CI checks it agrees with rule 1 wherever both apply, and
#      with index.jsonld's inLanguage always.
#
#   3. .md and .pdf have nowhere to carry a language, so they are declared below.
#      A publishable .md or .pdf missing from this list fails CI -- same doctrine
#      as .llms-exclude: silence is not an option.
#
# Format: <path>  <bcp47 tag>  # note
# Checked by scripts/check_index.py, enforced in CI.

theory/coordination-structures.md    en       # written in English
theory/holography-koopman.md         en       # English canonical; translated from the Chinese original
theory/holography-koopman.zh.md      zh-Hans  # the Chinese original: Chinese prose, English technical terms retained
theory/odd-relational-core.md        en       # English canonical; translated from the Chinese original
theory/odd-relational-core.zh.md     zh-Hans  # the Chinese original: Chinese prose, English technical terms retained
theory/state-as-closure.md           en       # English canonical; translated from the Chinese original
theory/state-as-closure.zh.md        zh-Hans  # the Chinese original: Chinese prose, English technical terms retained
essay.pdf                            en
